Source of the Apollo walkback limit (the problem card)
  Final Apollo 16 Lunar Surface Procedures, 16 March 1972, NASA Manned
  Spacecraft Center, Flight Crew Operations Directorate, section 3.6
  "EMU Consumables Data for Traverse Planning", p. 230: the traverse must
  allow a walkback to the lunar module after a rover failure, on the
  backpacks' (PLSS) consumables.
